Completion log:
- 2026-11-04: User reports occasional distortion/buzzing and requests prevention
  even if exact reproduction is unavailable. No supplied recording was tested.
- 2026-11-04: Configured latency alone does not establish real queue headroom.
  Add 96 ms pre-roll after native time initialization, with 128 ms config and
  200 ms lookahead. Earlier direct future-start experiment failed offsets.
- 2026-11-04: -1 dB compression overshot the settled test ceiling; -3 dB passes.
  Rapid native gain assignments need an explicitly tracked 15 ms envelope.
- 2026-11-04: Software-GPU failures exposed replaced-source observation and
  late timing assumptions. Monitor the stable master and the actual scheduling
  callback; retain PCM/recovery checks, not a steady-headroom claim on slow hosts.
- 2026-11-04: Publish and perform fresh live checks before final documentation.
- 2026-11-04: MDN compatibility data identifies cancelAndHoldAtTime as absent
  in Firefox. Use cancelScheduledValues with the existing explicit envelope;
  verify the optional API is unnecessary and deploy before final evidence.
